<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bentivoglio family</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bentivoglio were a family who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a> as unofficial lords for much of the 15th century, under the nominal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> of the Papal States. After Giovanni I briefly seized power in 1401, Annibale, Sante and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-ii-bentivoglio">Giovanni II Bentivoglio</a> dominated the city's government from the 1440s. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii">Pope Julius II</a> drove Giovanni II out in 1506, ending their rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bentivoglio-family.jpg" alt="Bentivoglio family" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MostEpic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_house_of_Bentivoglio.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
